bds 0,6 "ADS-B surface position"
date 2026-10-14
preamble
    ADS-B surface position (typecode 5-8). No altitude, aircraft is
    on the ground.
    Source: ICAO Doc 9871 (ICAO Annex 10 Vol. III) Mode S BDS register definition tables.

items

    TC "Type Code"
        definition
            ADS-B message type code.
        element 5
            unsigned integer
        remark
            5-8: surface position.

    MOV "Movement"
        definition
            Packed ground speed code.
        element 7
            unsigned integer
        remark
            Decoded to knots via a piecewise-linear lookup;
            0 means no information, 1 means stopped.

    TRACKSTATUS "Track Status"
        definition
            Validity of the track value.
        element 1
            table
                0: Not valid
                1: Valid

    TRACKCASE "Track Variant"
        definition
            Track value, present only when valid.
        case TRACKSTATUS
            1:
                group
                    TRACK "Track"
                        definition
                            Ground track.
                        element 7
                            unsigned quantity 360/128 "°"
            default:
                group
                    spare 7

    T "Time Sync Bit"
        definition
            Time synchronization indicator.
        element 1
            table
                0: Not synchronized
                1: Synchronized

    F "CPR Format"
        definition
            Compact position reporting format.
        element 1
            table
                0: Even
                1: Odd

    CPRLAT "CPR Latitude"
        definition
            Raw 17-bit CPR encoded latitude.
        element 17
            unsigned integer

    CPRLON "CPR Longitude"
        definition
            Raw 17-bit CPR encoded longitude.
        element 17
            unsigned integer
